# Vue 3 — `frontend*`

**Auth:** Access JWT only in Pinia; refresh in `httpOnly` cookie (e.g. scoped to `/api/v1/auth/refresh`). Cross-origin: `SameSite=None; Secure`. Router guards check **both** `isAuthenticated` and `role`; wrong role → `/unauthorized` (not `/login`). Route meta `requiresAuth`, `role` ∈ PATIENT | DOCTOR | ADMIN.

**Composition API:** `<script setup>` only; typed `defineProps`; composables `src/composables/use{Name}.ts`; no raw Axios in components — composables / Pinia actions only.

**Layout:** Components `src/components/{domain}/{Name}.vue`; pages `src/pages/{patient|doctor|admin}/{Name}.vue`; stores `src/stores/{name}.store.ts`; API `src/services/{name}.service.ts`. Parse API JSON with PascalCase wire keys; map to camelCase in services only (`api-json-pascal-case.mdc`). Tailwind only (no inline styles). Validate forms client-side; user-facing errors sanitized (no raw API errors).

**Buttons (consistent chrome):** Prefer `DynButton` with registered style templates — do not use raw `<button>` with ad-hoc Tailwind in primitives. Primary/secondary CTAs: `hosp.popup.button.primary` / `hosp.popup.button.secondary` (`inline-flex min-w-40 h-12`). Page forms may alias `hosp.page.button.*` (same chrome). Place actions in a flex row (`justify-end` on full-page forms, `justify-center` in popups) — never stretch CTAs full-width unless a design explicitly requires it. Toolbar/hero: `hosp.button.primary` / `secondary`. Config-driven pages: `type: 'button'` + `styles.styleTemplate` (see `bookAppointmentPage.ts`, `triagePopupPage.ts`).

**Popups:** Use `GlobalPopup` + declarative `*-popup` page configs (`usePopupStore` / `open-*` services). Never build success/confirm overlays inside primitives. See `frontend-popups.mdc`.

**Component ids:** Every `id` in page/config TS must be **unique within the file** (required for UI metadata merge). See `ui-component-ids.mdc`; run `npm run check:ui-ids`.

**Agora:** Tokens only from backend; channel = appointment UUID (not raw user IDs); handle token refresh mid-call; degrade to audio when network poor; on `onUnmounted`, close tracks and `client.leave()`.
